    "text": "To determine how many guppies Jason needs to buy per day, we need to calculate the total number of guppies consumed by the moray eel and the betta fish, and then sum these amounts.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of guppies the moray eel eats per day:\n\\[\n20 \\text{ guppies}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of guppies the betta fish eat per day. Since there are 5 betta fish and each eats 7 guppies per day, we multiply the number of betta fish by the number of guppies each eats:\n\\[\n5 \\times 7 = 35 \\text{ guppies}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the number of guppies eaten by the moray eel and the betta fish to find the total number of guppies needed per day:\n\\[\n20 + 35 = 55 \\text{ guppies}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Jason needs to buy \\boxed{55} guppies per day.",
